        "info": "The method of past conjugation varies depending on the type of verb or adjective. Here's a basic overview:\n\nRegular Verbs (Vowel Stems):\nFor verbs whose stems end with a vowel, you add \"-았/었\" to the stem.\n먹다 (to eat) -> 먹었어 (ate)\n\nRegular Verbs (Consonant Stems):\nFor verbs whose stems end with a consonant, you add \"-았/었\" to the stem, following the same rules as in the present tense. The vowel sound added depends on the final consonant.\n일어나다 (to wake up) -> 일어났어 (woke up)\n놓다 (to put) -> 놓았어 (put)\n\n하다 Verbs:\nFor verbs ending with \"하다,\" you replace \"하다\" with \"했어\" for the past tense.\n공부하다 (to study) -> 공부했어 (studied)\n\nIt's important to note that irregular verbs and adjectives may have their own unique patterns in the past tense. ",
